## Hyundai Home Shopping Network Corporation financial statements, 6 years: Revenue became 1.88x and operating income 0.69x

The consolidated financial statements in the 2020–2025 annual reports that Hyundai Home Shopping Network Corporation (057050) filed with Korea's DART electronic disclosure system, laid out by year. Figures from the 2026 half-year report cover a different period and are shown separately. **Every figure below is taken as filed in the DART submissions; there is no interpretation or outlook.** Amounts are in Korean won (KRW; bn = billion, tn = trillion).

### 1. Income statement — across the six years revenue became 1.88x and operating income 0.69x

| Fiscal year | Revenue | Revenue change | Operating income | Op. income change | Operating margin | Net income |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 2.02tn | — | 189.4bn | — | 9.4% | 152.1bn |
| 2021 | 2.10tn | +3.91% | 140.1bn | −26.05% | 6.7% | 140.9bn |
| 2022 | 2.10tn | +0.30% | 110.6bn | −21.03% | 5.3% | 57.5bn |
| 2023 | 2.06tn | −1.77% | 60.0bn | −45.81% | 2.9% | 136.2bn |
| 2024 | 3.85tn | +86.66% | 130.1bn | +117.05% | 3.4% | 174.2bn |
| 2025 | 3.79tn | −1.65% | 130.8bn | +0.49% | 3.5% | 114.7bn |

Revenue was largest in 2024 at KRW 3.85tn and smallest in 2020 at KRW 2.02tn among the six years. It fell from the previous year twice: 2023 (−1.77%), 2025 (−1.65%).

Operating income was largest in 2020 at KRW 189.4bn and smallest in 2023 at KRW 60.0bn. The operating margin was highest in 2020 at 9.4%.

**Net income was largest in 2024 at KRW 174.2bn and smallest in 2022 at KRW 57.5bn.**

### 2. Financial position — equity became 2.09x

| Fiscal year | Total assets | Total equity | Debt ratio | Current ratio |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2020 | 2.69tn | 1.79tn | 50.0% | 148.0% |
| 2021 | 2.60tn | 1.88tn | 38.1% | 179.2% |
| 2022 | 2.78tn | 1.96tn | 42.0% | 159.8% |
| 2023 | 3.43tn | 2.58tn | 32.9% | 247.4% |
| 2024 | 5.18tn | 3.84tn | 34.9% | 267.9% |
| 2025 | 4.97tn | 3.75tn | 32.5% | 259.8% |

The debt ratio was highest in 2020 at 50.0% and lowest in 2025 at 32.5%.

Over the same period total assets went from KRW 2.69tn to KRW 4.97tn (1.85x), and **total equity went from KRW 1.79tn to KRW 3.75tn and became 2.09x.**

The current ratio was above 100% in all six years, ranging from 148.0% to 267.9%.

